(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The full C API's layouts (queue 269; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 269\"; 262's DECISION (a), the user"] [4 1 "// 2026-11-10, and 268's DECISION (a), 2026-11-11). Without Py_LIMITED_API, CPython 3.14.10's Include/ reads objects in"] [5 1 "// place: Py_TYPE(o)->tp_flags (PyTuple_Check and the other subclass checks), PyList_Type.tp_new, PyTuple_GET_ITEM's"] [6 1 "// ob_item, PyList_GET_ITEM's ob_item array, PyBytes_AS_STRING's ob_sval, PyFloat_AS_DOUBLE's ob_fval. So:"] [7 1 "//"] [8 1 "//   - a type's handle is a PyTypeObject (PyHeapTypeObject's 936 bytes, or the world's static struct of a type"] [9 1 "//     Include/ names) filled as CPython's: tp_name, the sizes, tp_flags, tp_base, tp_bases, tp_mro, tp_dict, and its"] [10 1 "//     function slots (a type made from a spec its C functions, a pyi type the natives of the generic protocol);"] [11 1 "//   - a tuple's, list's, bytes' and float's handle is a mirror: the object's CPython layout in the world's memory,"] [12 1 "//     made when C first sees the object and kept in step with the pyi value at the C boundary, both ways (as PyPy's"] [13 1 "//     cpyext does): from Go to C before the world is called and when a native returns (the objects it touched), from"] [14 1 "//     C to Go when the world returns and when a native receives a mirrored object (its first use in the native). A"] [15 1 "//     container's mirror holds references to its items' handles, as CPython's container holds its items: a slot C"] [16 1 "//     writes (PyTuple_SET_ITEM, PyList_SET_ITEM) steals the reference C gave, a slot Go changes holds a new one and"] [17 1 "//     gives the old one back, and a mirror released gives its items back."] [18 1 "//"] [19 1 "// Layouts from Include/cpython/{object,tupleobject,listobject,bytesobject,floatobject}.h (CPython 3.14.10, LP64; the"] [20 1 "// PSF's license, LICENSE.md); the slots' offsets are Objects/typeslots.inc's."] [36 1 "// PyTypeObject's and PyHeapTypeObject's fields (offsets, LP64)"] [38 28 "// sizeof(PyHeapTypeObject)"] [70 1 "// slotOffsets is Objects/typeslots.inc (slot id -> the sub-struct's field offset, -1 for none, and the type's field"] [71 1 "// offset), from CPython 3.14.10's headers by gcc (offsetof, LP64)."] [81 1 "// the heap type's own sub-structs (PyHeapTypeObject's as_async, as_number, ...), by the type's field that points"] [82 1 "// at one"] [86 1 "// builtinTpFlags are CPython 3.14.10's tp_flags of the types Include/ names (type.__flags__, python3 3.14.10)."] [102 1 "// typeFlags is t's tp_flags as a C reader sees them: CPython's own for the types Include/ names, a type's made from a"] [103 1 "// spec or by PyType_Ready its own, else the subclass bits, BASETYPE and HEAPTYPE pyi knows, READY, the version tag,"] [104 1 "// IMMUTABLETYPE for a static type, and HAVE_GC for a heap type."] [107 52 "// inherit_special: the base's fast-subclass bits"] [121 1 "// cTpName is tp_name: a C type's own, a heap class's __name__, a static type's module-qualified name outside builtins."] [132 1 "// genericSlots are the natives a pyi type's function slots point at (the generic protocol's functions of the same"] [133 1 "// signature), by slot id: C calling Py_TYPE(o)->tp_repr(o) calls PyObject_Repr."] [139 1 "// fillTypeObject writes t's PyTypeObject at a (its handle: the head is written by the caller; the fields of a"] [140 1 "// PyHeapTypeObject's size, or of a static struct's)."] [170 2 "// the function slots: a C type's own (its spec's or PyType_Ready's, inherited), else the generic natives"] [176 57 "// tp_doc: the spec's copy (queue 270b)"] [178 3 "// ht_name, ht_qualname (queue 270b: test_type_from_ephemeral_spec reads them)"] [181 3 "// ht_module (queue 521: _decimal's find_state_left_or_right reads it in place, pycore_typeobject.h's inline"] [182 3 "// _PyType_GetModuleState), the module PyType_FromModuleAndSpec named, kept for the process as the type is"] [227 1 "// classNew reports whether t's __new__ is a class statement's (the first dictionary of its MRO holding __new__ is a"] [228 1 "// pyi class's, not a built-in's or a C type's): its tp_new is then CPython's slot_tp_new (Objects/typeobject.c,"] [229 1 "// type_new's tp_new for a class whose namespace defines __new__, which its subclasses inherit), the class's __new__"] [230 1 "// called, not its built-in base's (_pickle's load_newobj calls cls->tp_new: a list or tuple subclass's __new__,"] [231 1 "// test_descr's test_reduce_copying, a NamedTuple's, test_enum's tuple subclasses)."] [244 1 "// storeSlot writes the function fn into the slot id of the type object at a (its sub-struct's field when the type"] [245 1 "// has that sub-struct)."] [258 1 "// loadSlot reads the slot id of the type object at a (0: none, or no sub-struct)."] [271 1 "// ---- mirrors ----"] [273 1 "// mirror is the CPython layout of a tuple, list, bytes, float, int or str in the world's memory, a handle's."] [275 17 "// 't' tuple, 'l' list, 'b' bytes, 'f' float, 'i' int, 'u' str"] [276 17 "// the pyi object (a subclass's instance too: its built-in part is mirrored)"] [277 17 "// a tuple's or list's slots as last synchronized"] [278 17 "// a bytes' contents as last synchronized"] [279 17 "// the synchronization epoch of the last copy from C"] [280 2 "// a str's (queue 270, capi_unicode.go): its kind, ASCII flag and characters' address; a str PyUnicode_New made"] [281 2 "// (fresh) keeps a copy of its characters to see what C writes"] [290 2 "// held are the references mirrors hold on their items' handles because Go put the item there (a reference C"] [291 2 "// wrote into a slot is C's own): \"C holds the only reference\" (a brand-new object) is a count less these of 1"] [294 28 "// the mirrors a native (or a closure) used: synchronized to C when it returns"] [298 1 "// mirrorKind is the layout o's handle mirrors (0: a proxy's head only) and the bytes it needs."] [312 19 "// PyByteArrayObject (queue 270: PyByteArray_AS_STRING, GET_SIZE)"] [331 3 "// PySetObject (py-capi-1122: PySet_GET_SIZE reads used): fill 16, used 24, mask 32, table 40, hash 48, finger"] [332 3 "// 56, smalltable 64 (8 entries of 16 bytes), weakreflist 192"] [338 1 "// longDigits are an int's absolute value in CPython's 30-bit digits, least significant first (none for 0)."] [350 1 "// writeLong writes an int's PyLongObject fields at a (Include/cpython/longintrepr.h, 3.14: lv_tag is the digits'"] [351 1 "// count shifted by 3 with the sign in the low bits, 0 positive, 1 zero, 2 negative; then the digits)."] [369 1 "// asFloatValue is a float's (or a float subclass's instance's) value."] [383 1 "// newMirror writes o's layout at a (its handle, the head written) and records the mirror."] [402 31 "// ob_shash: -1, not computed"] [409 31 "// ob_hash: -1, not computed"] [416 31 "// hash: -1, not computed"] [421 1 "// syncToC writes the pyi value's state into its mirror (the slots Go changed: a new reference to the new item, the"] [422 1 "// old one's given back)."] [427 3 "// a set's size: fill and used (its table is Go's)"] [433 3 "// a bytearray: ob_size, ob_alloc, ob_bytes, ob_start (Include/cpython/bytearrayobject.h); its storage a block of"] [434 3 "// the world's, made again when it grows"] [516 1 "// syncFromC copies what C wrote into its mirror to the pyi value (the slots C changed; a NULL slot is a nil item, as"] [517 1 "// CPython's NULL until C fills it), and does so for the mirrors its items name, once an epoch."] [546 3 "// C's slots as last synchronized: C changed nothing, so Go's value stands (Python code a native ran may have"] [547 3 "// resized the list since: gh-72054's __index__ popping from it, test_slice's getindicesex_seq), written to C"] [548 3 "// when the native that uses it returns"] [580 10 "// resized from C: not provided (PyByteArray_Resize is a native)"] [603 1 "// holdRef and unholdRef are a mirror's reference to an item Go put in it, and its giving back."] [623 1 "// cOnly reports whether C holds the only reference to the handle h (its count, less the mirrors' own, is 1)."] [626 1 "// rawObj is the object a handle names without synchronizing it (nil for NULL)."] [635 1 "// freeMirror releases a mirror's own memory and its items' references (its handle released)."] [655 1 "// syncAllToC writes every mirror's pyi state into C (before the world is called: Python code may have changed any)."] [662 1 "// syncUsedLists writes to C the lists' mirrors the natives used since the outermost entry into the world (usedLists)"] [663 1 "// whose length Python code changed, C's own writes taken first: a native that ran Python code returns (that code may have"] [664 1 "// resized a list C reads in place, PyList_GET_SIZE's ob_size: gh-92930's persistent_id clearing the list _pickle's"] [665 1 "// batch_list_exact walks, test_pickle's test_evil_pickler_mutating_collection, \"list changed size during iteration\")."] [669 25 "// released since"] [679 1 "// usedLists are the lists' mirrors natives used (touch) since the outermost entry into the world (World.Call, worldDepth"] [680 1 "// its nesting)."] [686 1 "// syncAllFromC copies every mirror's C state to its pyi value (when the world returns to Python)."] [694 1 "// nativeEnter and nativeLeave bracket a native's (or a closure's) run: what C wrote is copied to Go on the first use"] [695 1 "// of a mirrored object in it (fromHandle), and the mirrors it used are written back to C when it returns."] [716 1 "// touch marks a mirrored handle as used by the running native."] [728 1 "// ---- C types over a built-in base (268's DECISION (a), the user 2026-11-11) ----"] [730 1 "// born is a C type's instance over a built-in base (a type a spec or PyType_Ready made, deriving from list, tuple,"] [731 1 "// bytes or float): its memory is the world's, tp_basicsize bytes (and its items'), the built-in part a mirror of the"] [732 1 "// pyi value at its head, the extension's part C's after the base's size. The Go value is an instance of the type"] [733 1 "// keeping a built-in value, as a Python class deriving from the built-in keeps one; the record rides on it"] [734 1 "// (py.SetInstanceExt). Its memory lives as a C-born object's (queue 268): until Go collects the instance, then its"] [735 1 "// tp_dealloc runs on the world's next entry."] [743 1 "// bornKind is the mirrored layout of t's built-in base (0: none of them)."] [756 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over int (its mirror a PyLongObject's)"] [759 15 "// queue 270b: a spec over an exception (no mirror: C reads its fields through functions)"] [765 1 "// bornOf is o's record when o is a C type's instance over a built-in base (nil: none)."] [777 1 "// bornHandle is such an instance's handle: its memory's address, in the maps again (a count of 0: unowned until the"] [778 1 "// C entry ends; its mirror written from Go, which may have changed it meanwhile) when it had left them."] [795 1 "// bornNew is tp_alloc for a C type over a built-in base: the instance of sub with nitems items (a tuple's or bytes'),"] [796 1 "// a new reference."] [823 1 "// bornValue is the built-in value of a C type's instance over a built-in base its base's __new__ makes from the"] [824 1 "// arguments (queue 270b: a spec over int without tp_new, HeapCTypeWithBasesSlot(5)): the base's own value, or for an"] [825 1 "// exception the exception of sub itself."] [845 1 "// bornWith makes the instance of sub keeping the built-in value v (for an exception, v is the instance), its memory"] [846 1 "// the world's: tp_basicsize bytes (and nitems items') or the mirror's size, the built-in part mirrored."] [895 1 "// allocObj is tp_alloc's generic allocation of t (PyType_GenericAlloc): a C-born object, an instance over a built-in"] [896 1 "// base, or a type object's memory (type's own tp_alloc: a heap type C fills, then PyType_Ready's)."] [899 3 "// a type object (a C metaclass's too, queue 270b: its basicsize, the C tail after the PyHeapTypeObject)"] [926 1 "// rawTypes are the